## Why This Is Asked
Tests threat modeling and practical controls for log integrity across cloud boundaries, a common fintech risk.

## Key Concepts
- Log integrity, STRIDE/PASTA, SBOM, log signing, KMS, append-only storage, WORM, cross-cloud replication, SIEM/SOAR, tabletop exercises

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo code for signing log entries
function signLogEntry(entry, key) {
  const signature = crypto.sign("SHA256", Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(entry)), key);
  return { entry, signature };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify integrity of logs during audits across clouds?
- How would you coordinate key rotation and revocation in a distributed SIEM?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design privacy-conscious telemetry for a multi-tenant SaaS, balancing observability with isolation and auditability.

## Key Concepts
- Data minimization, per-tenant isolation, and role-based access controls
- Edge-to-central telemetry security, encryption in transit/rest
- SBOMs, reproducible builds, code signing, and attestation
- Runtime integrity checks and tabletop incident validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// PII redaction example for telemetry payload
function redact(payload){
  const safe = {...payload};
  if (safe.userEmail) safe.userEmail = 'REDACTED';
  return safe;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement per-tenant key management and rotation?
- What are the observability vs privacy trade-offs and how would you validate them in practice?
